      "outcome": "ready",
      "summary": "Seven ordered scenarios demonstrate the sac-246 snippet shelf on the real temporary Worker environment declared in context/runtime-capabilities.json (temporary-environment-v1: one D1 binding, one R2 binding, built assets, target:remote browser). Scenario 1 provisions and migrates the environment and shows the empty one-screen app. Scenario 2 is the main flow (save Greeting and Sign-off, read each body, refresh, delete Sign-off, Greeting remains) with D1 and R2 readback captured at its end. Scenario 3 must run immediately after scenario 2 with cloud data untouched, satisfying the human's 16:57 instruction to use the direct fresh-context continuity proof rather than the design's seeded fallback. Scenario 4 shows both bad-input rejections with unchanged storage, scenario 5 shows markup preserved as plain text with matching R2 bytes, scenario 6 shows real failed-action messages produced by an out-of-band API delete against a stale browser page, and scenario 7 captures final D1/R2 correspondence and then removes the temporary resources. All browser scenarios use one browser session, a fresh context per scenario, and a fixed 1440x900 desktop viewport against the same temporary origin. Storage proof always precedes cleanup. Design step 5 fault-injection checks (paused writer, injected put/cleanup failures) remain implementation tests and are deliberately not used as demo evidence, since tests do not demonstrate the application. No provider write beyond the declared temporary environment is requested, and no merge, release, or production deployment is implied.",
      "payload_key": "implementation/workflow:99426d9b-cda7-4db4-9136-692a95a0b090:e08fdf64-e2dc-42d5-b7e6-ab0a11607241:run:1/480aef4c406713fc1dd69851e94b3cd9ac3d49968417562e7197560fd9ffad0d/demo-review.json",
